.\" Maintained source, not generated. Update alongside command changes.
.TH ZI 1 "October 2026" "Zi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zi \- manage Zsh plugins, snippets and completions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zi
.I command
.RI [ arguments ...]
.br
.B zi ice
.I modifiers ...
.br
.B zi
.RI [ modifiers ...]
.B for
.I plugin ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Zi runs as a function in the current Zsh session after sourcing
.BR zi.zsh .
It installs and loads plugins and snippets, manages completions and records
selected shell changes for reporting and unloading.
Plugin code and ice hooks execute with the permissions of the current user.
Review their sources before loading them.
.PP
This is a concise offline reference. Detailed options, annexes and configuration
recipes are maintained at https://wiki.zshell.dev/.
.SH GETTING STARTED
Zi requires Zsh and Git. Follow the installation instructions at
https://wiki.zshell.dev/docs/getting_started/installation/.
The repository README documents the current installer and how to review it.
Source the installed
.B zi.zsh
from your Zsh configuration before calling Zi; it is not a standalone program
to invoke through Bash or sh.
For a local checkout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
source /absolute/path/to/zi/zi.zsh
zi light zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions
zi light z-shell/F-Sy-H
.RE
.fi
.PP
Loading a remote plugin installs it if needed. Choose plugins and their order
deliberately; these commands execute downloaded code.
.SH LOADING
.TP
.B load
Load a plugin with tracking and reporting. Accepts an owner/repository name
or an absolute local plugin directory.
.TP
.B light
Load without full tracking or reporting. The
.B \-b
option retains bindkey tracking. Do not rely on full unload restoration.
.TP
.B unload
Unload a tracked plugin. Restores recorded state, not every possible side
effect of arbitrary plugin code.
.TP
.B snippet
Load a local or remote snippet.
.TP
.B ice
Set modifiers for the next load operation. Modifiers control selection,
installation and lifecycle hooks. Quote arguments containing shell syntax.
.PP
.nf
.RS
zi ice depth"1"
zi light zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions
.RE
.fi
.TP
.B for
Apply inline modifiers to a sequence of plugins.
.PP
.nf
.RS
zi light-mode for zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions z-shell/F-Sy-H
.RE
.fi
.TP
.B icemods, recall
List registered modifiers, or reconstruct a command from saved modifiers.
.SH MAINTENANCE
.TP
.B update, self-update
Update plugins or snippets, or update and compile Zi itself.
Consult command help before changing update strategy or parallelism.
.TP
.B delete
Remove a plugin or snippet from disk. This is distinct from unloading it
from the shell. Review the target before confirming deletion.
.TP
.B compile, uncompile, compiled
Compile plugins, remove compiled files, or list compiled plugins.
.TP
.B create
Create a plugin. This may interact with GitHub; inspect the prompts before
accepting repository creation.
.TP
.B edit, glance
Edit a plugin using EDITOR, or view its source.
.TP
.B cd, run
Enter a plugin or snippet directory, or run a command in a plugin directory.
.TP
.B add-fpath
Append a directory to fpath; the \-f option prepends it.
.TP
.B srv, module
Control a service (stop, start, restart, next, quit), or manage optional zpmod.
.TP
.B env-whitelist
Specify parameter names or patterns that unloading leaves unchanged.
.SH COMPLETIONS
.TP
.B compinit
Initialize or refresh completions.
.TP
.B clist, completions, csearch
List installed completions, or search plugins for available completions.
.TP
.B cenable, cdisable
Enable or disable a completion.
.TP
.B creinstall, cuninstall, cclear
Install or uninstall a plugin's completions, or clear stray completions.
.TP
.B cdlist, cdreplay, cdclear
List, replay or clear recorded compdef calls. Replay after compinit.
.SH INSPECTION
.TP
.B version
Show the version; also accepts \-V or \-\-version.
.TP
.B help, analytics, man
Show command help (\-h or \-\-help), the diagnostic menu, or this manual.
.TP
.B subcmds
Show commands registered by loaded annexes.
.TP
.B zstatus, loaded, list, ls
Show overall status, loaded plugins (loaded and list), or snippets (ls).
.TP
.B status, report, times
Show repository status, recorded loading changes, or plugin loading times.
.TP
.B changes, recently, bindkeys
Show a plugin's Git log, recently changed plugins, or recorded key bindings.
.TP
.B stress
Exercise a plugin under combinations of shell options. This executes plugin
code and is a diagnostic action, not a security sandbox.
.TP
.B dstart, dtrace, dstop, dreport, dunload, dclear
Start tracking session changes (dstart or dtrace), stop tracking, report them,
revert recorded changes, or clear the report.
.SH FILES AND ENVIRONMENT
ZI[BIN_DIR] identifies the source checkout. ZI[HOME_DIR] contains installed
plugins, snippets and other persistent manager data.
Explicit ZI directory settings take precedence.
.PP
Fresh layouts use $XDG_DATA_HOME/zi, $XDG_CACHE_HOME/zi and
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zi for data, cache and configuration.
Unset, empty or relative XDG bases fall back to ~/.local/share, ~/.cache and
~/.config, respectively.
An existing ~/.zi layout is retained; sourcing Zi does not automatically
migrate it. When both layouts exist, the sourced installation helps select
the active one.
.PP
ZPFX is the prefix for additional software, defaulting to the polaris
subdirectory of ZI[HOME_DIR]. Set directory overrides before sourcing Zi.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The focused test matrix covers Zsh 5.8.1, 5.9 and 5.9.2 on Linux and macOS.
It does not establish compatibility with every plugin, older Zsh versions,
BSD or Cygwin. Existing runtime fallbacks for older versions remain.
